Yet Another Annoying Death - a neutral priest, my first priest for
about three years. Had completed the Mines, which provided a BoH, 2
magic lamps, one for light and one which had wished up the Staff of
Mispelling, +3 mithril, +oID and a wand of fire, in case any nasties
needed to be scared away by a certain word, so I was feeling pretty
hopeful about this one. However, I should have realised the RNG was
setting me up.

So, I'd finished the mines, and had just past the oracle when I
started to feel the pangs of hunger. Rather than reach into my BoH
(which contained ample food), I decided to head up into Sokoban and
sample the food on offer there, while hoping for an "oR. Right next to
the stairs on the first level was a tin, which I proceeded to open and
digest - bad mistake. Just as my finger was plunging down on the y
key, I noticed the word "chickatrice" on the screen...

DYWYPI?

And because it's sokoban, I don't even have a chance of snatching this
equipment out of the statue in a later game.

In five years of playing, this is the first time I've found a tin of
cockatrice, or any meat that can harm me for that matter. I'll have to
be more careful in future!

